    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>f(x)</m>, below.  It may be to your
advantage to simplify  first.</p>
<p><me>\displaystyle f(x) = \frac{x^5}{e^x}</me></p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{5x^{5-1}e^{x}-x^{5}\ln\mathopen{}\left(e\right)e^{x}}{e^{2x}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>f'(x) = \frac{(5 x^{-1})(e^x) - (x^5)  (e^x)}{e^{2x}}.</me></p>
</solution>
